rsion.detected.count line: a JSON pattern $.event = &quot;x&quot; is an EXACT match not a prefix, so one diversion is one datapoint (WN956 re-reported one diversion 62 times in ~7s in real prod).<br/>namespace OagEventSource/Ingest. Previously ZERO filters existed on either group -- which is how 134,579 discarded messages went uncounted while every dashboard read healthy<br/>FORWARD-ONLY AND THEREFORE NEVER A BASELINE: a metric filter evaluates events as they are INGESTED and cannot backfill. The historical figure is a SEPARATE dual-key Logs Insights lane (infra/scripts/baseline-ingest-drops.sh, retention 3653 days) whose own non-vacuity assertion is that over a window spanning the 2026-07-29 rename the dual-key count is STRICTLY GREATER than the logClass-only count<br/>DUAL KEY ($.logClass || $.category) FOR ARTEFACT DRIFT, NOT HISTORY: a lane running an older bundle emits the pre-d8e452b field name and a single-key pattern is silently blind to it -- the DEFECT-OAG-030 / 063 / 071 class<br/>NO DIMENSION: delta-054's table listed streamId, which as a metric DIMENSION mints one CloudWatch metric per flight (a cost and throttling defect). streamId lives in the LOG LINE; the per-lane split comes free from having two filters<br/>defaultValue 0 ON EVERY FILTER so a ZERO IS AN OBSERVATION rather than a missing-data hole -- the difference between a measured control and a blind one<br/>[NO LONGER APPLIES - DEFECT-OAG-084] the dependsOn-the-Lambda edge existed because a LAMBDA log group is auto-created on first invocation so a fresh-stage filter create could race it. The Lambda lane is deleted; the ECS Service DECLARES its log group by name (section 9.7 logging.name), so it is not invocation-created and no filter here carries that edge<br/>DEPLOY-ROLE GRANT: logs:PutMetricFilter/Delete/Describe added to the EXISTING CloudWatchLogsOagScoped statement -- delta-054 said 'no IAM change' and the apply would have returned AccessDenied. Three actions, one statement, ZERO ARN wideni